      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "The transfer function of a system Z(s) = V(s)/I(s) = (s+3)/s. The system is at rest for t < 0. What will be the value of V(t) for t ≥ 0, if i(t)=3u(t), where u(t) is a unit step?",
      "options": [
        "e^(-t)",
        "2e^(-3t)",
        "3e^(-3t)",
        "4e^(-t)"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "With Z(s) = V(s)/I(s) = s/(s+3) and I(s) = L{3u(t)} = 3/s, V(s) = s/(s+3) * 3/s = 3/(s+3). Inverse Laplace gives V(t) = 3e^(-3t) for t ≥ 0, which is option (c).",
